.Sh DESCRIPTION
The low-level MAC functions documented on this page are deprecated.
Applications should use the new
.Xr EVP_MAC 3
interface.
Specifically, utilize the following functions for MAC operations:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_new 3 No to create a new MAC context.
.It Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_free 3 No to free the MAC context.
.It Xr EVP_MAC_init 3 No to initialize the MAC context.
.It Xr EVP_MAC_update 3 No to update the MAC with data.
.It Xr EVP_MAC_final 3 No to finalize the MAC and retrieve the output.
.El
Alternatively, for a single-step MAC computation, use the
.Xr EVP_Q_mac 3
function.
.Pp
The
.Vt CMAC_CTX
type is a structure used for the provision of CMAC (Cipher-based Message
Authentication Code) operations.
.Pp
.Fn CMAC_CTX_new
creates a new
.Vt CMAC_CTX
structure and returns a pointer to it.
.Pp
.Fn CMAC_CTX_cleanup
resets the
.Vt CMAC_CTX
structure, clearing any internal data but not freeing the structure
itself.
.Pp
.Fn CMAC_CTX_free
frees the
.Vt CMAC_CTX
structure and any associated resources.
If the argument is NULL, no action is taken.
.Pp
.Fn CMAC_CTX_get0_cipher_ctx
returns a pointer to the internal
.Vt EVP_CIPHER_CTX
structure within the
.Vt CMAC_CTX .
.Pp
.Fn CMAC_CTX_copy
copies the state from one
.Vt CMAC_CTX
structure to another.
.Pp
.Fn CMAC_Init
initializes the
.Vt CMAC_CTX
structure for a new CMAC calculation with the specified key, key length,
and cipher type.
Optionally, an
.Vt ENGINE
can be provided.
.Pp
.Fn CMAC_Update
processes data to be included in the CMAC calculation.
This function can be called multiple times to update the context with
additional data.
.Pp
.Fn CMAC_Final
finalizes the CMAC calculation and retrieves the resulting MAC value.
The output is stored in the provided buffer, and the length is stored in
the variable pointed to by
.Fa poutlen .
To determine the required buffer size, call with
.Fa out
set to NULL, which stores only the length in
.Fa poutlen .
Allocate a buffer of this size and call
.Fn CMAC_Final
again with the allocated buffer to retrieve the MAC.
.Pp
.Fn CMAC_resume
resumes a previously finalized CMAC calculation, allowing additional
data to be processed and a new MAC to be generated.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn CMAC_CTX_new
returns a pointer to a new
.Vt CMAC_CTX
structure or NULL if an error occurs.
.Pp
.Fn CMAC_CTX_get0_cipher_ctx
returns a pointer to the internal
.Vt EVP_CIPHER_CTX
structure, or NULL if an error occurs.
.Pp
.Fn CMAC_CTX_copy ,
.Fn CMAC_Init ,
.Fn CMAC_Update ,
.Fn CMAC_Final
and
.Fn CMAC_resume
return 1 for success or 0 if an error occurs.
.Sh HISTORY
All functions described here were deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0. For
replacements, see
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_new 3 ,
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_free 3 ,
.Xr EVP_MAC_init 3 ,
.Xr EVP_MAC_update 3 ,
and
.Xr EVP_MAC_final 3 .
